# Heracles

Heracles is the son of Zeus and the mortal Alcmene, a granddaughter of
Perseus. Hera hated him from before his birth: she delayed Alcmene's
labour so that his cousin Eurystheus would be born first and rule over
him. At Eurystheus's command he performed the labours, and at his death he
was made a god and married Hera's daughter Hebe.

## His ancestors

Every ancestor the first account of each birth names, nearest first, each
once. Through Zeus the line reaches Kronos and Rhea, then Uranus and Gaia,
who in Hesiod comes into being after Chaos and is born of no one. Through
Alcmene it reaches her grandfather Perseus, whose father is Zeus again.
The Greek names are put into Latin letters by the `greek` package, and
each ancestor links to its article in [[wikipedia]].

```hql#eval
import myth.kb
import myth.beings
import myth.genealogy as family
import myth.wikipedia

articles = wikipedia.articles(@[[wikipedia]].body.unwrap_or(""))

family.lineage(kb.parentage(), "heracles")
| map(a => kb.being(a.being) | map(b => {
    generation: a.generation,
    name: b.name,
    greek: b.greek,
    latin: b.latin(),
    kind: b.kind,
    wikipedia: wikipedia.article(articles, b.id) | map(w => w.link()) | unwrap_or(""),
  }))
| somes
| Table(columns = ["generation", "name", "greek", "latin", "kind", "wikipedia"])
```
